{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And when you reap.</b> Just as you give from the altar of peace-offerings that are said to belong to HaKadosh Baruch Hu, so too shall you give to the poor and to the stranger from the harvest of your land, for the honor of HaKadosh Baruch Hu." "<b>When you reap.</b> This excludes what was reaped by Canaanites — for if they reaped it while it was a Canaanite's and it then became converted, it is exempt from פאה." "<b>The harvest of your land.</b> To include legumes." "<b>You shall not wholly reap the corner of your field.</b> Rabbi Shimon says: whether he gives at the beginning, or in the middle, or at the end, he has fulfilled his obligation, and it is considered פאה, provided that he does not give less than one part in sixty." "<b>To reap.</b> Stated last, to include the one who plucks."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:27.270197975Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}